1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,755
No Autowired? This still works.

2
00:00:01,835 --> 00:00:03,080
This Spring-managed service

3
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,720
has one constructor.

4
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,620
Spring selects it automatically.

5
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:08,592
Autowired is optional here.

6
00:00:08,672 --> 00:00:10,760
Spring reads its parameter type:

7
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,700
PaymentGateway. In our context,

8
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:14,727
one matching bean is available.

9
00:00:14,807 --> 00:00:16,200
Spring supplies that instance

10
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,560
through the constructor.

11
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:19,433
The service keeps the reference.

12
00:00:19,513 --> 00:00:20,660
Now an order calls

13
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:22,280
the injected gateway.

14
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:23,960
Our test checks the same instance

15
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:25,707
and the returned result.

16
00:00:25,787 --> 00:00:27,280
Creating an object with new

17
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:30,200
still means supplying arguments yourself.

18
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:31,000
Let Spring wire

19
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,921
the beans it manages.

20
00:00:34,921 --> 00:00:36,012
Thanks for watching.

